# TypeScript strictness

Keep `"strict": true`. Do not loosen other compiler flags unless the user asks. The type checker must exit 0 before the work is reported done. Validate data from outside the typed boundary (third-party responses, request input, environment) with a schema or a type guard before trusting it.
